A("# Grand tournament: every daily indicator single and pair x every option structure. Full backtest verdict (2026-11-12)\n")
A('**Question (Sam, 2026-11-12):** "test literally every single possible indicator/strategy to develope the single most effective options strategy and backtest everything to prove profitability"\n')
A(f"**Status:** complete. Frozen plan: `claude/grand-tournament-daily-options-preregistration-2026-11-12.md` (SHA-256 `{fr['prereg_sha256']}`, frozen {fr['frozen_utc']}, before any strategy P&L from this code existed). No frozen file changed afterwards (all hashes re-checked). Robustness work done after the results is marked post hoc.\n")
A(f"**Label: {W['label'].upper() if False else W['label']}** for the winner (8 of 8 gates) and for the top-10 ensemble (6 of 6 gates). Unlike today's intraday tests, the winner clears every pre-registered gate out of sample. It is not proof of profitability, and one post hoc check shows how it could be false.\n")
A(f"**Headline.** Out of {U['eligible']:,} eligible configurations, the one picked without using 2020-2026 data was: **when RSI(14) is below 35 and DeMarker(14) is below 0.30 at the close, buy a 0.30-delta call 2 to 3 weeks from expiry at that close and sell it at the next close.** Out of sample (2020 to 11 Nov 2026) it made {p(bo['mean'])} of the premium per trade in the model (90% interval {p(bo['lo'])} to {p(bo['hi'])}, {bo['n']} trades, monthly Sharpe {bo['sharpe']:.2f}), which is {u(o['usd_1.0'])} dollars per contract per trade at the house spread on an average premium of {o['avg_risk']:.0f} dollars. The same signal on plain shares made {o['shares_bp']:+.0f} bp per one-day trade out of sample and was positive in every period back to 2001. The catch: every option price is a model. If the calls really cost about {100*lad['LONG30']['breakeven_entry_iv_overpay']:.0f}% more implied volatility at entry than the model assumes (and that extra is not recovered at exit), the option profit is zero; and {100*wp['top15_share']:.0f}% of the out-of-sample dollars came from 15 of the {bo['n']} trades.\n")
A("**Research, not advice.** I am not a licensed financial advisor. Every option number is a Black-Scholes model (PROXY), not market quotes. A backtest cannot prove future profit; this one shows a rule chosen on 2010-2019 kept working in 2020-2026 inside a pricing model.\n")
A("## Bottom line\n")
A(f"- **\"Every possible\" was replaced by the widest fixed universe I could run:** 192 indicator readings from 67 families on daily bars, all 18,528 singles and pairs, 5 holding periods (1 to 10 sessions), 2 entry conventions, 3 side rules and 8 option structures: 4,446,720 configurations, of which {U['eligible']:,} trade often enough to judge.")
A(f"- **What wins is one family: buy calls after an oversold reading, hold 1 to 5 days.** All ten of the top-ranked configurations are long calls, long-only; eight include an oversold reading and two are trend rules. Nothing bearish, nothing neutral and no multi-leg structure reached the top.")
A(f"- **Most of the universe loses.** Share of eligible configurations with a positive out-of-sample mean: {100*U['share_pos_oos_mean_by_cost']['0.0']:.0f}% before costs, {100*U['share_pos_oos_mean_by_cost']['0.25']:.0f}% at a quarter of the house spread, {100*U['share_pos_oos_mean_by_cost']['1.0']:.0f}% at the house spread, {100*U['share_pos_oos_mean_by_cost']['2.0']:.0f}% at twice it. Only {100*U['share_score_pos']:.1f}% had a positive Sharpe in both 2010-2014 and 2015-2019.")
A(f"- **Past rank did predict future rank this time.** Of the configurations positive in both earlier periods, {100*U['share_oos_pos_given_score_pos']:.0f}% were positive out of sample; the top 1,000 by score averaged an out-of-sample Sharpe of {U['top1000_oos_sharpe_mean']:.2f} and {100*U['top1000_share_oos_pos']:.0f}% of them were positive. In today's 5-minute tournament the same correlation was negative. Part of this is structural (condors and verticals lose in every period because of modelled costs), but the dip-buying family also held up on its own.")
A(f"- **The edge is in the underlying, which is the part I trust.** Shares bought at the signal close and sold at the next close: " + ", ".join(f"{r['cc_bp']:+.0f} bp ({r['period']}, {r['n']} trades)" for r in B["shares_core"]) + ". It is concentrated in stressed markets: out of sample " + ", ".join(f"{r['shares_bp']:+.0f} bp with {r['bucket']}" for r in RW["by_vix_oos"]) + ". IWM stopped responding after 2014.")
A(f"- **The option wrapper is the part I cannot verify.** Paying 5% more implied volatility at entry cuts the out-of-sample result from {p(lad['LONG30']['base_oos'])} to {p(lad['LONG30']['over5_oos'])} per trade; 10% more turns it to {p(lad['LONG30']['over10_oos'])}, and the 2010-2019 results to {p(lad['LONG30']['over10_dev'])} and {p(lad['LONG30']['over10_val'])}. Real quotes on signal days are the missing evidence.")
A(f"- **What I would do:** treat this as the best forward-test candidate the project has produced, not as a funded strategy. Run it in shadow mode on SPY and QQQ, logging the real ask at the close on signal days and the real bid at the next close for the 0.30-delta and 0.80-delta calls. About {o['trades_per_year']*134/246:.0f} SPY and QQQ signals a year means roughly a year for a first honest read; buying end-of-day chain history for the ~340 past signal dates would answer it in a day.\n")
A("## What was tested\n")
A("| Part | As run |\n|---|---|")
A("| Data | SPY, QQQ, IWM daily bars (Yahoo, unadjusted), 2000-05-26 to 2026-11-11; Cboe VIX, VXN, RVX; 13-week T-bill yield |")
A("| Indicators | 192 daily readings in 67 families: 91 trend / momentum / breakout (moving averages and crosses, MACD, ROC, Donchian, DMI/ADX, Supertrend, Parabolic SAR, Ichimoku, Aroon, Keltner, Bollinger, Heikin-Ashi, TRIX, KAMA, Hull, Vortex, OBV, CMF, candles, gaps, VIX trend, relative strength, bonds), 70 reversal (RSI 2/3/5/14, Connors RSI, Stochastic, Williams %R, CCI, Bollinger, IBS, down-streaks, n-day lows, z-scores, MFI, DeMarker, Fisher, divergences, candles, VIX spikes), 27 neutral filters (volatility, ADX, volume, range, squeeze, weekday, season), 4 calendar (turn of month, option-expiry week, pre-holiday, first day) |")
A("| Signal sets | Every single and every pair (both must agree): 18,528 |")
A("| Entry | At the close of the signal day. STATE: whenever the agreement is on. FRESH: only the first day it is on. Sides: bullish only, bearish only, or both |")
A("| Exit | Time only: 1, 2, 3, 5 or 10 sessions later at the close. One position per ETF at a time. No stops, targets or adjustments |")
A("| Structures (PROXY) | Long call or put at 0.80, 0.65, 0.50, 0.30 delta; debit vertical (0.60 / 0.30); credit vertical (0.30 / 0.15); long straddle; iron condor (0.20 / 0.10). Expiry: first Friday at least 14 days out (21 for 5-session holds, 35 for 10) |")
A("| Costs | Per leg: 3.88 bp of the underlying (x1.5 for QQQ, IWM) scaled by delta, 1-cent floor, plus 0.65 dollars commission per contract per side. Grid: mid, 0.25x, 0.5x, 1x (house), 2x |")
A("| Periods | Development 2010-2014, validation 2015-2019, out of sample 2020-01-01 to 2026-11-11 |")
A("| Selection | Score = the lower of the 2010-2014 and 2015-2019 monthly Sharpe at the house spread. Highest score wins. Out of sample is read once |\n")
A("**Units.** \"% of risk\" is net dollars divided by the capital at risk in the trade (the premium for long options). \"bp\" is basis points of the ETF price (1 bp = 0.01%). Dollars are per contract per trade. Sharpe is computed on monthly sums of per-trade return on risk across the three ETFs.\n")
