A(f"\n- **Term structure.** On panic days short-dated volatility is above VIX (8 Apr 2025: VIX9D 67.6 against VIX 52.3) and collapses faster. Pricing with the interpolated term structure lowers the out-of-sample result to {p(RW['ts']['oos']['mean'])}; it survives.")
A(f"- **Three days.** The entries before the 13 Mar 2020, 24 Mar 2020 and 9 Apr 2025 rebounds supply about half of the mean. Without them the result is {p(RW['base_no_events']['oos']['mean'])} (p = {RW['base_no_events']['oos']['p']:.3f}). Those days are what the rule is built to catch, so removing them is harsh, but it shows the dependence.")
A(f"- **Volatility level is the weak point.** The whole option edge equals about {100*lad['LONG30']['breakeven_entry_iv_overpay']:.0f}% of entry implied volatility (roughly 2 to 3 volatility points on a signal day). The model's 0.30-delta call volatility is an extrapolation from two calibration points at 0.65 delta; an error of that size is plausible in either direction.")
