A("## Deviations, notes and limits\n")
A("| ID | What | Effect |\n|---|---|---|")
A("| D1 | Expiry wording. The plan says \"first listed Friday at least 14 calendar days out (previous session if the Friday is a holiday)\". The frozen code requires the expiry date after the holiday move to be at least 14 days out, so a Good Friday week is skipped. | 5 of 518 winner trades; out-of-sample mean 17.18% under the code's reading, 17.24% under the other. |")
A("| D2 | The ensemble contains one duplicated member (see above). The frozen rule was followed. | Ensemble without it: +14.9% per trade, Sharpe 1.29. |")
A("| D3 | `final.py`, `robust.py`, `extras.py`, `verify.py`, `make_verdict.py` and the VIX9D file were added after the freeze. | They read frozen code and saved results; no frozen file changed. All robustness results are post hoc. |")
A("| D4 | The best-per-structure list written by the frozen `run.py select` covered only structures that reached its top-3,000 table; `final.py` recomputed it over every eligible configuration. | Reporting only. |")
A("| D5 | The first rerun comparison was made before the rerun had finished and was repeated after it completed. | V3 above is the repeated check. |")
A("| D6 | Period boundaries in the data loader were set to 2015 and 2020 before the freeze (an earlier draft of the loader had 2014 and 2019). | Before any P&L; not a deviation from the frozen plan. |\n")
A("- Every option number is PROXY: Black-Scholes on VIX-family closes with a straight-line skew, no real quotes or fills, no early exercise. The 0.30-delta call sits outside the two calibration points.")
A("- Entry at the close needs RSI and DeMarker computed a few minutes early, and assumes a fill at the modelled close price on days when option spreads are at their widest. The 2x-spread column is the only allowance for that.")
A("- The winner was chosen from 1.67 million configurations, but only on 2010-2019; the 2020-2026 figures are not selection-inflated. The post hoc tables (strikes, neighbours, VIX buckets, ETF cuts) are descriptive.")
A("- 2020-2026 contained three violent rebounds that paid most of the profit. A period without one would look like 2023 (+2.3% per trade).")
A("- Not tested: real quotes; intraday and weekly bars; three-way combinations; other parameters; stops, targets and adjustments; calendars, butterflies, ratio and naked short structures; 0-2 DTE; single stocks; earnings and news; position sizing; taxes. Yahoo data through 11 Nov 2026 was taken as delivered.\n")
A("## Files\n")
A("`grand_tournament.zip`: frozen code (`pull.py`, `prep.py`, `ind.py`, `options.py`, `engine.py`, `stats.py`, `run.py`, `tests.py`), post-freeze scripts, `PREREG.md`, `freeze.json`, raw data, `leaderboard_top3000.csv`, `baselines.csv`, `select.json`, `final.json`, `robust.json`, `extras.json`, the winner and ensemble trade ledgers. The 30 result blocks (all 4.4 million configurations) are regenerated by `python run.py full` in about 4 minutes.\n")
